Kario's patch to QuickJS-ng 0.18.0: debugger hooks for kario-jsrt
(29-app-development.md §3, the debugger of apps installed in developer
mode). Like QuickJS-ng, this patch is under the MIT licence (LICENSE in the
QuickJS-ng tree); Copyright (c) 2026 The Kario authors.

- JS_SetDebugHandler: frames entered while a handler is set run every
  instruction through it (a second dispatch table: frames entered without
  one pay nothing); debugger statements (a new opcode, OP_debugger) and
  thrown exceptions, with whether a try on the stack catches them, call it
  in any frame. Code compiled while a handler is set, or after
  JS_SetDebugPositions (an app a debugger may attach to while it runs),
  records the position of every statement, where breakpoints and steps
  stop.
- JS_DebugFrameCount, JS_DebugFramePoint, JS_DebugFrameInfo,
  JS_DebugFrameLines, JS_DebugFrameVariables, JS_DebugSetVariable: the
  frames on the stack, their positions, line tables, arguments, locals and
  closure variables.
- OP_debugger renumbers the opcodes after it: the bytecode version and the
  version string (0.18.0+kario.1) change with it, so bytecode of the
  unpatched engine is never loaded.

Applied by make jsrt (Makefile) and by Yocto's quickjs recipe.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hooks for Kario's own debugger protocol]

